  "manual": {
    "notes": [
      "BAPTISM EVENT MISATTACHED (research workflow, 2026-07-03): 'baptism 18 Jul 1842, Tipperary, Ireland' cannot belong to William — he was born Jan 1859 in Massachusetts, 17 years AFTER this baptism. The Irish-origin source collections (Ireland Select Births & Baptisms; Ireland Catholic Parish Registers) instead fit his own father, John Murphy — an 1842 Tipperary baptism would make John about 17 at William's 1859 birth. Detach this event from William; needs direct record review to confirm reassignment to John.",
      "PROBABLE UNDOCUMENTED SECOND MARRIAGE: the tree gives William 11 children, but only 7 (Emeline Jane, Julia Maria, William Francis, Abbie Teresa, Robert Emmet, Charles Henry Sr, Walter Joseph) are attributed to wife Bridget Mary Gilligan, who died in 1898. Four more (a duplicate 'Walter Joseph', William Henry, Grace Agnes Murphy Sullivan, Olive Catherine Murphy O'Malley) are listed only under William, who lived until 1943 — consistent with a second, unnamed wife after 1898. Decisive records: MA marriage index 1898-1910 for 'William J. Murphy', and the 1900/1910/1920 federal censuses.",
      "Birthplace 'Rockland' is anachronistic-but-not-wrong for a Jan 1859 birth: Rockland wasn't incorporated (split from Abington) until 1874 — a contemporary record would read 'Abington.' Worth trying both town names in further searches.",
      "'Residence: Kerry St.' carries no date or town in the export; likely Rockland, Weymouth, or Brockton (the family's known towns) but unconfirmed which."
    ]
  }
